                        "entry_id": "8049bfd4-5898-3dfd-9933-854a8c86d619",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who revolts or who does something revolutionary; revolutionist."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c4a05d0-245c-49d3-b1b1-a31556ebceb6",
                                "sense_id": "ee9da508-786f-35db-b2d6-a7cfc1ff2eba",
                                "text": "Skirmishers from Baía marched on to help the revolutioneers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "112a2674-8a41-4fbe-b46a-4e4dd0a272c1",
                                "sense_id": "ee9da508-786f-35db-b2d6-a7cfc1ff2eba",
                                "text": "In any country, whenever you secretly participate or openly assist, by whatever means, the revolt against the existing social system, you are a revolutioneer, an outlaw, and the State punishes you severely."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4c92a8ea-ed48-4d20-8a5e-0ec1a96fff31",
                                "sense_id": "ee9da508-786f-35db-b2d6-a7cfc1ff2eba",
                                "text": "Thorstein Veblen, who hated businessmen per se, and whose writings influenced the New Deal revolutioneers, gave \"C grades to all his pupils at Columbia University."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "14c87756-fa48-4061-aa79-110618d8169e",
                                "sense_id": "ee9da508-786f-35db-b2d6-a7cfc1ff2eba",
                                "text": "French revolutioneers wore cheap pants with coloured stripes, so they called themselves Sans Culotte because they looked more like parading in pyjamas."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
